--TEST--
Every `break`/`continue` level with no statically-known target is `E0475`, never a panic — `nvs_types::locals::check_exit_level`, and PHP refuses all five at compile time too
--FILE--
<?nvs
int $depth = 2;
array<string> $rows = ["a"];
foreach ($rows as string $r) {
    // A level resolves to an enclosing statement at compile time, so it
    // cannot be computed — PHP stopped accepting this in 5.4.
    break $depth;
    // Levels count from 1: the innermost enclosing statement.
    break 0;
    // One loop encloses this, so 3 names two statements that do not exist.
    break 3;
}
switch ($depth) {
    case 2:
        // A `switch` is a level, but it has no back edge to continue: a
        // level landing on one looks further out, and there is no loop.
        continue 1;
    default:
        echo "x\n";
}
// The same rule with no level written at all — level 1 of nothing.
break;
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0475]: a `break` level must be an integer literal
  --> %s:7:11
  |
7 |     break $depth;
  |           ^^^^^^ this is computed at run time
  = help: `break N;` names the N-th enclosing loop or `switch` at compile time, so N has to be written out

error[E0475]: `break 0` leaves nothing
  --> %s:9:11
  |
9 |     break 0;
  |           ^ the innermost enclosing statement is level 1

error[E0475]: `break 3` names more levels than enclose it
   --> %s:11:11
   |
11 |     break 3;
   |           ^ 1 enclosing loop/`switch` here, so the highest level is 1

error[E0475]: `continue 1` names no enclosing loop
   --> %s:17:18
   |
17 |         continue 1;
   |                  ^ every statement at or outside this level is a `switch`
   = help: `continue` needs a loop to start the next iteration of; a `switch` has none, so a level landing on one looks further out and finds nothing here

error[E0475]: `break` is not inside a loop or `switch`
   --> %s:22:1
   |
22 | break;
   | ^^^^^^ no enclosing loop or `switch` to leave

error: aborting due to 5 errors
